WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
(audience applauds)
- I know you're dating.

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:02.400
- Yes.
- You're dating,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.881
so are you getting married
and do you wanna tell us now?

00:00:04.881 --> 00:00:06.560
(laughs) Okay, no.
- (laughs) Girl talk!

00:00:08.264 --> 00:00:09.720
You know what?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.380
Not to get weird, but I think that,

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.010
also, it's important to say this,

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.910
especially to our younger fans

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.150
and younger generations of women.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.970
I come from the Bible Belt
in Oklahoma, very proudly so,

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.880
but with that means that
you're supposed to get married,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.120
have 2.5 kids, and live in
the white picket fence house,

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.490
and I didn't choose that for
my life, I had other goals,

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.110
and at first, I was always ashamed,

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.230
like I shouldn't tell people

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.590
that, maybe, I'm not sure
about having children or

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.300
even, maybe, getting married,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.620
and I've had great men in my life.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.350
I've got a great one right now.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.920
Marriage might be the deal, it might, but

00:00:46.981 --> 00:00:49.930
it hasn't been what's
defined me or driven me,

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:51.924
and, for a long time, I
was shameful about it.

00:00:51.924 --> 00:00:53.461
(audience applauds)
- Yeah, 'cause especially

00:00:53.461 --> 00:00:54.608
from where we're from.

00:00:54.608 --> 00:00:56.240
- Because of where we're from.
- Yeah.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.090
- And also, thank you.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.610
- Did people always think you were gay?

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.160
People thought I was gay forever.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.150
- I've had some boyfriends

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.659
to make me wish I was gay, but no.

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:07.927
(everyone laughs)
- Me too, me too.

00:01:07.927 --> 00:01:10.847
- No, I'm not, and as
far as people will go,

00:01:10.847 --> 00:01:11.910
"You're not gonna have a child?"

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.160
and it's almost like, oh, selfish,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.890
but I take care of a lot of
kids, I have many cousins.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.490
I have godchildren I take care of,

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.300
and this is also important to say.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.923
As an adopted child,

00:01:24.468 --> 00:01:26.830
if I have that so desire one day,

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.630
and I wake up and I say,
"Maybe I missed the boat,"

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:31.630
or "Maybe I wanna do that,"

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.260
there's been so many great
examples of women who've

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.700
done that and I would just adopt a child.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.327
There's many people out there.
(audience applauds)

00:01:40.327 --> 00:01:43.880
- The thing about that, too,
is one, that you're picked.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.810
My mom just got stuck with me.
(Kristin laughs)

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.000
You were picked.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.418
- They do say you're chosen.
- They got to pick you.

00:01:48.418 --> 00:01:49.824
- Yeah.
Yeah, that's really cool.

00:01:49.824 --> 00:01:51.010
- It's a special feeling

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.660
and I've always known
about my adoption and

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:56.270
my family, they're all chemical
engineers and real tall

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:57.233
and they don't sing.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:57.233 --> 00:01:59.630
They don't sing and
they should never sing,

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.020
actually, ever.
(audience laughs)

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.850
But I don't do math, but
we learn from each other.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.803
- That's awesome, that's so great.

